course: dictionary
lesson: 12738
title: Clues from droppings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Droppings are the solid waste, or poo, that animals and birds leave behind. You can use the words around droppings as clues to work out what left them.
explain: «We found small black droppings under the shed, so a mouse may live there.» Small, black and under the shed are the clues. Mouse droppings are small and dark, so the sentence helps you guess the animal.
explain: Scientists and nature explorers study droppings to find out which animals live in an area. Droppings are useful evidence, but you must never touch them. «Do not touch the rabbit droppings; wash your hands after playing outside.»
fact: Droppings means the solid waste of animals and birds.
fact: Bird droppings, mouse droppings, rabbit droppings and sheep droppings are common phrases.
fact: Droppings can help you find out which animals live in an area.
fact: Droppings can carry germs, so always wash your hands after being outside or after handling pets.
exercise: «We found small black droppings under the shed.» What are droppings? | Pieces of old wood | Small stones that fall from the roof | *Solid waste left by animals and birds | Seeds scattered by the wind
exercise: «We found small black droppings under the shed, so a mouse may live there.» What can droppings help you find out? | How old the shed is | *Which animals live in an area | Which day it will rain | What colour the walls are painted
exercise: Why should you wash your hands after touching sheep droppings? | Sheep droppings are always clean | They make your hands smell of flowers | *They can carry germs | Washing is only needed at lunchtime
test: «The white marks on the car were bird droppings.» Which phrase means the waste of rabbits? | *Rabbit droppings is wrong, so choose rabbit noises | Rabbit feet | Rabbit droppings | Rabbit fur
test: Lila sees a pile of droppings in the field. What should she do first? | *Leave them alone and wash her hands after being outside | Eat her snack right next to them | Kick them across the grass | Pick them up with her bare hands
exam: Which is the best reason to be careful around droppings? | They only appear in the sea | *They can carry germs | They are made of plastic | They are always sweet-smelling
